# CRITICAL CLINELULES FOR WINDOWS & LOCAL LLM

## ABSOLUTE TERMINAL RULES (STRICTLY ENFORCED)
- NEVER use `&&` in terminal commands. It crashes PowerShell 5.1.
- NEVER run build, test, or server commands (`npm run build`, `ng build`, `ng serve`, `npm start`). The user handles builds manually.
- NEVER run `cd` combined with other commands. Just execute commands from the current directory.
- NEVER use Linux commands (`ls`, `rm`, `cat`, `touch`, `grep`, `export`). Use Windows/PowerShell equivalents (`dir`, `Remove-Item`, `Get-Content`, `Select-String`).

## COMMAND SYNTAX RULES
- Separate sequential commands with `;` instead of `&&`.
- Always use backslashes `\` for file paths, never forward slashes `/`.
- Prefer direct file editing (write_to_file) over running terminal commands to view or change code.

## CODE STANDARDS
- **Angular:** Use Standalone components, Signals, and modern control flow (`@if`, `@for`).
- **React:** Use Functional Components with Hooks.
- **Context Protection:** NEVER read or search inside `node_modules`, `dist`, `.git`, or `.angular`.